rpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":229941,"global_rank":112655},{"name":"Adjective-Object/doc-csv","owner":"Adjective-Object","html_url":"https://github.com/Adjective-Object/doc-csv","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"csv to docx forms","topics":[],"score":229932,"global_rank":112662},{"name":"amarisch/kubeflow-training","owner":"amarisch","html_url":"https://github.com/amarisch/kubeflow-training","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":229932,"global_rank":112663},{"name":"DylanDmitri/all","owner":"DylanDmitri","html_url":"https://github.com/DylanDmitri/all","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"help my computer dead","topics":[],"score":229931,"global_rank":112667},{"name":"Sohojoe/baby-muzero","owner":"Sohojoe","html_url":"https://github.com/Sohojoe/baby-muzero","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"MuZero, without the complexity ","topics":[],"score":229919,"global_rank":112675},{"name":"kuzentio/mitra","owner":"kuzentio","html_url":"https://github.com/kuzentio/mitra","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":2,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":229918,"global_rank":112681},{"name":"kevinslin/dotfiles","owner":"kevinslin","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinslin/dotfiles","stars":3,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Some helpful dotfiles","topics":[],"score":229904,"global_rank":112697},{"name":"Sagar-py/aethra-django","owner":"Sagar-py","html_url":"https://github.com/Sagar-py/aethra-django","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"